      "knowledge_point_id": "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int (2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nRearranging the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
