      "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their respective captured worked solutions. However, q-106463 contains an authored source error: its opening sentence says the parabola passes through (-5,-7), whereas the image labels (-10,7). The subsequent calculation correctly uses (-10,7), producing the correct answer. Independently: q-106463 has (y+5)^2=-12(x-2), generated by option 2. q-84854 eliminates t to give (x+5)^2=-4(y+2). q-72157 uses the chain rule, giving -28 cos^6(x) sin(x). q-38547 has g(0)=-2, left limit 0, and right limit -2, so only II holds. q-104283 has f(-5)=3 by right continuity, so the requested limit is 3-6=-3. q-18284 has cofactor C22=4, giving inverse entry 4/(-16)=-1/4. q-141365 follows the cosine addition formula. For q-74421 and q-114346, intersecting the given line with the perpendicular through the external point gives (2,-5) and (-1/5,7/5), respectively. For q-114600, integrate 2x-(1/2)sin(2x). For q-74400, the integrand is 4sin(4x). For q-114688, integrate -cos(8x) from 0 to pi/4, obtaining 0. For q-74410, the integrand is cos(2x). For q-114712, the integrand simplifies to cos(x/2), whose integral over [0,pi] is 2. For q-102757, the vectors are collinear and their determinant is zero. For q-31398, substitution u=ln(x) gives (2/9)(ln(x))^(3/2)+C, equivalent to the selected radical expression on the real domain x>=1. No submitted-grade evidence or earlier answer is supplied; each MA answer is supported by its own captured worked solution.",
